# burrows-amazon
#
# The chain, once a day: look up new barcodes, decide what each product's state is,
# then send the ones that qualify. Each step is safe to run on its own and safe to
# run twice; push re-checks the brand, the match and the stock immediately before
# every write, so a stale decision cannot reach Amazon.
20 5 * * *   /opt/burrows-amazon/run.sh match    >> /var/log/burrows-amazon-match.log 2>&1
10 6 * * *   /opt/burrows-amazon/run.sh populate >> /var/log/burrows-amazon-populate.log 2>&1
30 6 * * *   /opt/burrows-amazon/run.sh push     >> /var/log/burrows-amazon-push.log 2>&1
40 6 * * *   /opt/burrows-amazon/run.sh audit    >> /var/log/burrows-amazon-audit.log 2>&1

# Stock is the safeguard: it corrects quantities against what Amazon actually holds,
# and withdraws anything we have stopped intending to list. It writes nothing when
# nothing has moved.
*/15 * * * * /opt/burrows-amazon/run.sh stock    >> /var/log/burrows-amazon-stock.log 2>&1

# Reads Amazon back and records what it is unhappy about.
*/30 * * * *  /opt/burrows-amazon/run.sh health   >> /var/log/burrows-amazon-health.log 2>&1
